%I A399346 #10 Oct 03 2026 17:24:02
%S A399346 1,2,2,2,3,3,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,5,5
%N A399346 Placid Platypus function PP(n): Minimal number of states of all 2-symbol Turing machines that print exactly n ones then halt.
%H A399346 Busy Beaver Challenge Wiki, <a href="https://wiki.bbchallenge.org/wiki/Placid_Platypus">Placid Platypus</a>
%H A399346 James Harland, <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.5555/1151785.1151794">The Busy Beaver, the Placid Platypus and other Crazy Creatures</a>, CATS '06: Proceedings of the 12th Computing: The Australasian Theroy Symposium, Volume 51, pp. 79-86, 2006.
%F A399346 a(n) <= n.
%F A399346 If n > A028444(m), then a(n) > m.
%e A399346 a(8) = 4 because a 4-state 2-symbol machine 1RB1RZ_1LC0RD_1LA1LB_0LC1RD print exactly 8 ones when halt. And no machine with smaller state count print exactly 8 ones when halt.
%Y A399346 Cf. A028444 (Busy Beaver), A060843 (Frantic Frog).
%K A399346 nonn,more,new
%O A399346 1,2
%A A399346 _Zhuorui He_, Sep 29 2026
